#. type: Title =
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.45.3.adoc:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "Git v2.45.3 Release Notes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.45.3.adoc:8
msgid ""
"This release merges up the fix that appears in v2.40.4, v2.41.3, v2.42.4, "
"v2.43.6 and v2.44.3 to address the security issues CVE-2024-50349 and "
"CVE-2024-52006; see the release notes for these versions for details."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.45.3.adoc:12
msgid ""
"This version also backports various small fixes accumulated on the 'master' "
"front during the development towards Git 2.46, the next feature release."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.45.3.adoc:15
#, no-wrap
msgid "Fixes since v2.45.2"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.45.3.adoc:18
msgid "Git-GUI has a new maintainer, Johannes Sixt."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.45.3.adoc:22
msgid ""
"Tests that try to corrupt in-repository files in chunked format did not work "
"well on macOS due to its broken \"mv\", which has been worked around."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.45.3.adoc:24
msgid "The maximum size of attribute files is enforced more consistently."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.45.3.adoc:27
msgid ""
"Unbreak CI jobs so that we do not attempt to use Python 2 that has been "
"removed from the platform."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.45.3.adoc:32
msgid ""
"Git 2.43 started using the tree of HEAD as the source of attributes in a "
"bare repository, which has severe performance implications.  For now, revert "
"the change, without ripping out a more explicit support for the attr.tree "
"configuration variable."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.45.3.adoc:36
msgid ""
"Windows CI running in GitHub Actions started complaining about the order of "
"arguments given to calloc(); the imported regex code uses the wrong order "
"almost consistently, which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.45.3.adoc:39
msgid ""
"The SubmittingPatches document now refers folks to manpages translation "
"project."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.45.3.adoc:43
msgid ""
"\"git rebase --signoff\" used to forget that it needs to add a sign-off to "
"the resulting commit when told to continue after a conflict stops its "
"operation."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.45.3.adoc:47
msgid ""
"The procedure to build multi-pack-index got confused by the replace-refs "
"mechanism, which has been corrected by disabling the latter."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.45.3.adoc:50
msgid ""
"\"git stash -S\" did not handle binary files correctly, which has been "
"corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.45.3.adoc:54
msgid ""
"A scheduled \"git maintenance\" job is expected to work on all repositories "
"it knows about, but it stopped at the first one that errored out.  Now it "
"keeps going."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.45.3.adoc:58
msgid ""
"zsh can pretend to be a normal shell pretty well except for some glitches "
"that we tickle in some of our scripts. Work them around so that \"vimdiff\" "
"and our test suite works well enough with it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.45.3.adoc:62
msgid ""
"Command line completion support for zsh (in contrib/) has been updated to "
"stop exposing internal state to end-user shell interaction."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.45.3.adoc:65
msgid ""
"The documentation for \"git diff --name-only\" has been clarified that it is "
"about showing the names in the post-image tree."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.45.3.adoc:69
msgid ""
"The chainlint script (invoked during \"make test\") did nothing when it "
"failed to detect the number of available CPUs.  It now falls back to 1 CPU "
"to avoid the problem."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.45.3.adoc:73
msgid ""
"\"git init\" in an already created directory, when the user configuration "
"has includeif.onbranch, started to fail recently, which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.45.3.adoc:76
msgid ""
"The safe.directory configuration knob has been updated to optionally allow "
"leading path matches."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.45.3.adoc:78
msgid "An overly large \".gitignore\" files are now rejected silently."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.45.3.adoc:81
msgid ""
"Fix for an embarrassing typo that prevented Python2 tests from running "
"anywhere."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.45.3.adoc:84
msgid ""
"Varargs functions that are unannotated as printf-like or execl-like have "
"been annotated as such."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.45.3.adoc:89
msgid ""
"The \"-k\" and \"--rfc\" options of \"format-patch\" will now error out when "
"used together, as one tells us not to add anything to the title of the "
"commit, and the other one tells us to add \"RFC\" in addition to \"PATCH\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.45.3.adoc:93
msgid ""
"When the user adds to \"git rebase -i\" instruction to \"pick\" a merge "
"commit, the error experience is not pleasant.  Such an error is now caught "
"earlier in the process that parses the todo list."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.45.3.adoc:98
msgid ""
"We forgot to normalize the result of getcwd() to NFC on macOS where all "
"other paths are normalized, which has been corrected.  This still does not "
"address the case where core.precomposeUnicode configuration is not defined "
"globally."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.45.3.adoc:102
msgid ""
"Earlier we stopped using the tree of HEAD as the default source of "
"attributes in a bare repository, but failed to document it.  This has been "
"corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.45.3.adoc:105
msgid ""
"An unused extern declaration for mingw has been removed to prevent it from "
"causing build failure."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.45.3.adoc:108
msgid ""
"A helper function shared between two tests had a copy-paste bug, which has "
"been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.45.3.adoc:111
msgid ""
"\"git fetch-pack -k -k\" without passing \"--lock-pack\" (which we never do "
"ourselves) did not work at all, which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.45.3.adoc:112
msgid "Also contains various documentation updates and code clean-ups."
msgstr ""
